  "title": "Plague epidemic risk in Russia reduced post-death of lab worker, WHO confirms",
  "summary": "The World Health Organization (WHO) reports that the risk of an epidemic in Russia has been significantly reduced after the sudden death of a lab technician, Darya Shipilova, who worked in a plague research institute in Siberia. The WHO highlights that the chances of the virus spreading in Russia are very low, despite the lab worker's death.",
